WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:06.060
Speaking of going forward to the election,
we actually have some what I think is overall

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:11.339
very good news and news that is extremely
triggering for the president of the United

00:00:11.339 --> 00:00:12.339
States, Donald Trump.

00:00:12.339 --> 00:00:17.200
The second and final presidential debate is
this Thursday, and candidate microphones will

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:22.330
be muted during the initial answer periods
when the other candidate is speaking.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:25.780
This is not going to apply during the open
discussion period.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.730
You're still going to have back and forth
during the open discussion.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:33.010
But as you might remember, during the first
presidential debate, Donald Trump just would

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.579
not stop talking, interrupting Joe Biden.

00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:41.359
It wasn't clear whether Trump was sort of
manically out bursting or whether it was a

00:00:41.359 --> 00:00:45.550
strategy to try to throw Biden off or a combination
of the two.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:50.620
But it made the debate worthless in terms
of hearing policy ideas, although it does

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:56.030
seem to have hurt Donald Trump in polling
because of his childish, petulant behavior.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:01.829
So when the we then after that first debate
had the Commission on Presidential Debates

00:01:01.829 --> 00:01:06.120
announce that what should have been the second
debate would happen be a video conference

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:10.270
because Trump had coronavirus and Trump said
not going to do it remote.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.120
They can silence you whenever they want.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:15.030
If you do that and he backed out of the debate
altogether.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.850
So we now have one debate to go.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:21.241
The last debate scheduled for Thursday night
and indeed, during the initial two minute

00:01:21.241 --> 00:01:27.490
answer periods, the microphone of the candidate
not speaking will be muted.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:32.590
The Commission on Presidential Debates said
in a statement that, quote, We realize after

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:36.960
discussions with both campaigns that neither
campaign may be totally satisfied with the

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.660
measures announced today.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:42.120
One may think they go too far and one may
think they do not go far enough.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:46.200
We are comfortable that these actions strike
the right strike, the right balance, and that

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.790
they are in the interest of the American people
for whom these.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:51.830
Debates are held.

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:56.920
Now, there were some people who soon after
the first debate and people started calling

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:00.380
for the muting of microphones, said a few
mute the mikes.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:01.610
It's not really a debate.

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:02.620
Few mute mikes.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:04.440
It's sequential talking points.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:05.670
It eliminates debate.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:09.150
It eliminates the possibility of a back and
forth.

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:15.510
This is a balanced approach in the sense that
of each fifteen minute block, four minutes

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:19.970
will be reserved exclusively for one candidate
or the other.

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:24.300
After the four minute period, two minutes,
two minutes for each candidate, then the microphones

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.300
are open.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:26.300
It's open discussion.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:30.190
So I think it will undeniably make the debate
more watchable.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:33.600
There are people wondering whether it's really
even better for Biden.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:38.310
One would imagine that letting Biden kind
of lay out his ideas uninterrupted will help

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:39.310
him.

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:40.310
And I think it would.

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:46.240
The counter is, does it help him more than
the damage Trump does by just talking over

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.930
Biden during those initial couple of minutes?

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.870
Biden could have helped himself by speaking
uninterrupted.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:56.350
But Trump really cratered in the polls after
that first debate.

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:59.930
In the end, again, there will be time for
both.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:04.420
Four of each fifteen minutes will be including
Mike muting.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:07.209
So it's a relatively small adjustment.

00:03:07.209 --> 00:03:11.660
Bottom line, these are the updated rules and
Donald Trump is already not pleased.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:15.380
He said yesterday to reporters after being
told about this change, I'll participate.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:19.590
I just think it's very unfair.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:24.450
Trump also spent time at a rally in Prescott,
Arizona, yesterday attacking the moderator

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:25.459
of this week's debate.

00:03:25.459 --> 00:03:26.910
Who is Kristen Welker?

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:27.980
Take a listen to that.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:30.190
The real great one.

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:32.830
Another great one.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:34.599
Kristen Welker.

00:03:34.599 --> 00:03:35.599
She's a radical Democrat.

00:03:35.599 --> 00:03:37.349
Look at him getting angry.

00:03:37.349 --> 00:03:38.349
She's a radical Democrat.

00:03:38.349 --> 00:03:40.300
She deleted her entire account.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:41.520
Everything is deleted.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.160
But I've known her.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:49.550
She's been screaming questions at me for a
long time, and she's so good.

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:51.380
So Trump attacking the moderator there.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:55.640
And then reportedly the president is also
not happy that, as he sees it, the topics

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:57.000
were changed.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:01.170
Trump kept saying the debate Thursday night
was on foreign policy.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:07.739
And now, for example, Corona virus is a topic
I always thought that foreign policy was not

00:04:07.739 --> 00:04:09.550
the subject of Thursday night's debate.

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:13.480
But Trump is angry, claiming they changed
the topics on him.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:17.390
So bottom line, I think there's a chance Trump
does back out.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.720
I would put it probably at about 20 percent.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:20.720
I hope he doesn't.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.490
I hope this debate does happen.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:26.490
But it's very funny how for months Donald
Trump had been saying, oh, Biden's going to

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:27.690
find a way out.

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:29.060
Biden's brain's not working.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:31.020
He can't handle debating me.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:34.010
And then it's Trump who bailed on debate number
two.

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:37.940
And it's Trump who's not pleased with the
guidelines for debate number three.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:42.180
Now, a serious question and a lot of people
are asking about this.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:46.710
Is Trump going to just try to interrupt anyway,
even if he's off, Mike?

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:50.199
My guess is if Trump tried to do it, yeah,
it would look very bad.

00:04:50.199 --> 00:04:54.400
But you would be able to probably hear Donald
Trump's voice if he tries to interrupt.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:55.400
Interrupt.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:05:00.740
Joe Biden picked up both by Joe Biden's microphone,
maybe as much as by the moderator's microphone.

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:03.310
So I think it's something Trump could do.

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:06.490
I think if he does it, it would look very,
very bad.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:10.460
And reports are that Trump's advisers and
people prepping him for the debate have been

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:16.460
advising him not to interrupt and to sort
of try to be more likable, even if Trump likes

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:20.750
the idea of being more liked, as I'm sure
his ego would, would like.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:24.290
Donald Trump has a very hard time controlling
himself, and Donald Trump has a very hard

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:28.470
time listening to people who give him advice
because he thinks he knows better than everybody.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:34.210
So my prediction is that in Nashville, 9:00
p.m. Eastern on Thursday night, which is when

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:35.500
the debate starts.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:40.220
My prediction is that Trump's behavior will
be very similar to what we saw in debate number

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:41.230
one at the beginning.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:42.720
He might be more under control.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:44.470
I think he will eventually lose it.

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:46.570
I hope you will watch the debate with me.

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:51.880
I will be streaming live on YouTube, Twitter
and Facebook, starting maybe 30, 45 minutes

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:53.250
before the debate.

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:58.669
Join me then and we will take it all in together.

00:05:58.669 --> 00:06:02.750
If you're not going to watch the debate, I'm
curious about why.

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:50.940
Let me know on Twitter where you can find
me at də pacman 

00:06:50.940 --> 00:07:35.840
The 
David Pakman Show at David Pakman dot com.

